    {
      "id": 35258,
      "name": "Mirrors",
      "slug": "mirrors",
      "batch": "Fall 2026",
      "url": "https://www.ycombinator.com/companies/mirrors",
      "changed_fields": [
        "industries",
        "long_description",
        "one_liner",
        "subindustry"
      ],
      "changes": {
        "industries": {
          "before": [
            "B2B",
            "Infrastructure"
          ],
          "after": [
            "B2B",
            "Engineering, Product and Design"
          ]
        },
        "long_description": {
          "before": "Your agent worked fine yesterday. Today it loops, drops context, or calls a tool with the wrong arguments, and you find out from a user.\r\n\r\nTeams shipping AI agents change prompts, models, and tools constantly, and the same failures keep coming back in production: context loss, loops, broken tool calls, regressions after a refactor.\r\n\r\nMirrors learns from your agent's production traces. It captures what worked and what failed in real sessions, then delivers the fix at runtime. Instead of waiting for someone to notice a regression and patch it by hand, the fix is applied automatically, so the same error never happens twice.\r\n\r\nBuilt for teams whose agents do things they can't undo, like issuing refunds, updating customer records, or sending outbound email.",
          "after": "Production agents handle many different customer workflows. Currently, when one handles a situation badly, an engineer reads the trace and patches the prompt. The next situation needs another exception. Soon, improving the agent becomes a recurring engineering job, and the prompt keeps growing.\r\n\r\nMirrors finds patterns in past runs and feedback. Engineers review guidance for a specific situation and preview where it would apply. Mirrors then delivers that guidance while the agent works, inside the team’s existing setup. The team can check whether the change improved the outcome.\r\n\r\nWe’re building Mirrors for engineering teams running customer-facing agents across varied workflows, so they can improve behavior without hardcoding every lesson in the global prompt."
        },
        "one_liner": {
          "before": "Fix your AI agent's errors at runtime, so they never happen twice",
          "after": "Steer AI agents in real time using lessons from production runs"
        },
        "subindustry": {
          "before": "B2B -> Infrastructure",
          "after": "B2B -> Engineering, Product and Design"
        }
      }
